    "finalText": "Everything is complete and verified. All 14 tests pass, style checks pass, and the database is left in a clean migrated state.\n\n**Implementation summary:**\n- `app/Models/Link.php` + migration — `links` table (unique 20-char `code`, `url`, `clicks` counter) persisted in MySQL read from `DB_*` env vars\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php` — create (generated 8-char code with retry on unique-violation races, 409 for duplicate custom codes), show, list (ascending by id with total), and 302 redirect with `clicks` increment\n- `bootstrap/app.php` — api routes registered with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are `/links` and `/r/{code}`, JSON forced for all error responses, `ValidationException` → 422 `{\"error\"}` and 404s → `{\"error\"}`\n- `start.sh` (executable) — runs `php artisan migrate --force` then serves foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` with `--no-reload`\n- README section covering endpoints and startup\n\n**Verified end-to-end via `sh start.sh`:** 201 creates (generated and custom codes), 409 duplicates, correct 302 `Location` header with exactly-once click increments, list order/total, and 422s for malformed JSON, invalid/missing URLs, and invalid codes. Data and click counts survived a full server restart."
